There is consensus that there are shortcomings, and people certainly
disagree on the priorities of them.  Yet, teams of people can work in
a hierarchical manner, if that's what it takes to get something
accomplished.  Other software, including games, are produced by teams
in various forms.  There is more than one person working on Crawl. The
current nethack dev team in its rough form has managed to crank out a
lot of good stuff over the years, before the Great Sleep.

This is another route of argumentation that has often come up here to
kill anything before it's started - the argument that a group of
people can't possibly get together and do anything reasonable to
continue progress on nethack.  This is unnecessarily defeatist and
doesn't jibe with reality.


